  "guide": "Open a customer with named requirements and a Unix-second deadline. Ingest only events from authorized sources, with a stable unique event_id and source reference; duplicate events are not reapplied. This service monitors deadlines while running. Connectors or agents submit documents/replies; it does not scrape email or watch arbitrary directories. Claim events, inspect the customer, use installed file actions to read approved files, then review each requirement with expected_revision. Questions are drafts only: send externally only through separately authorized tools. Link tasks and knowledge entries using links. Handoff requires accepted requirements and no unanswered questions. Claims expire; deduplicate work by event ID and acknowledge only after success. Actor labels route work within a trusted collection, not an authentication boundary. Pause stops new claims and notifications while preserving incoming events. Offline inbox is the default; optional HTTPS runner notifications require a reviewed network-enabled package and operator-supplied webhook/token secrets (see README). Notifications only wake a configured runner, never execute incoming instructions. MCP alone cannot wake an agent. Start the Rhyven daemon; opt into service autostart to monitor across reboots.",
  "tests": [],
  "display_name": "Customer Onboarding Monitor"
}
